xnu: MERLIN 0121 rate-limit the MSDC DMA-spill diagnostics (0118 print storm)

0118 prints EVERY DMA-spill event plus every changed byte range. With the
0120 native-geometry fix SpringBoard finally runs and does heavy rootfs
I/O, and every multi-block read spills 16 KB into the bounce canary
(programmed_len=49152, changed_envelope=[49152,65536) - the known
controller overrun, caught by the bounce buffer, no data corruption).
Result: 63,000+ events by t=280 s, a console/log print storm that starves
boot I/O - the device crawls (xpcproxy/fairplayd still exec'ing at
t=281 s per the bootlog-ci2 ring) and looks hung.

Restore the pre-0118 rate limit (print event 1 and every 1000th, full
detail including the RANGE lines on those) so the diagnostics stay
available without drowning the console.

Files:
  bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c    gate the 0118 spill prints

diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c
index f2cef92..80e9275 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c
@@ -1434,6 +1434,7 @@ msdc_transfer_once(uint64_t lba, uint32_t nblk, bool is_write)
 		if (bad != 0) {
 			uint64_t now_ns = 0;
 			msdc_spill_count++;
+			if (msdc_spill_count == 1 || (msdc_spill_count % 1000) == 0) {
 			absolutetime_to_nanoseconds(mach_absolute_time(), &now_ns);
 			const volatile uint8_t *bytes =
 			    (const volatile uint8_t *)mo.dma;
@@ -1491,6 +1492,7 @@ msdc_transfer_once(uint64_t lba, uint32_t nblk, bool is_write)
 				    (unsigned long long)msdc_spill_count,
 				    start, i);
 			}
+			}
 		}
 	}
 	msdc_wr(MSDC_INT, 0xffffffffu);
